            "gate": "overreach",
            "why": "77 spans stand where the grammar claims a construct and TiddlyWiki reads prose, down from 161 across the pragma zone and the directive separator. Asked of the parser, every one of them reads kind=text: no construct covers them, so they name real divergences rather than sub-tokenization inside a built whole. They fall into five families \u2014 26 from \\rules except rules turning the rules pragma off, which a static grammar carries no state for; 21 from a shortcut opener that wants no keyword where TiddlyWiki wants one; 16 from a style run the parser declines; 8 from an HTML document standing in a .tw; and 6 from an image with a blank source. Four of the five close with grammar work or a ruling; the first wants a decision."
